    "result_text": "The change is in, and all 4 tests in `bin/e2e` pass.\n\n- **Rounding:** live dues now round half to even (1.025 \u2192 1.02, 1.035 \u2192 1.04). I changed this in two places that must agree: `dueOf` in `rates/rates-api.ts`, which works the figure out exactly in whole numbers, and the server's `ClaimService.dueOf`, which now uses `HALF_EVEN`. The server one is what fixes a claim's figure when it's settled. Claims already settled keep the figure they were stored with.\n- **Per-claim due:** I moved the \"settled figure, otherwise the live due at the rate on the claim's date\" logic into one shared function, `claimDue` in `claims/claims-api.ts`. The claim rows and the person totals both use it, so they can't drift apart.\n- **Person due-total** (`people/people.ts`): it now adds up the rounded figures of the claims that count (open and settled), skips any that show n/a, and shows 0.00 when nothing counts. If the person's grade has no rate today it shows n/a, unless one of their counting claims has a settled figure. In that case it shows the sum of whatever figures exist.\n- **Sheet due-total:** still everyone's due-totals added up, with n/a skipped.\n\nNo database change was needed.",
